# Rust build artifacts
/target/

# Backup files from `cargo fmt` etc.
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC debug info (Windows)
*.pdb

# Editor / OS junk
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Neovim writes its own log beside the directory it was started in, and the
# Workbench starts it on the project root -- so opening that mode here drops a
# file in the repo every run. It is this machine's, not the project's.
nvim.log

# Local onehand runtime state / persisted config written next to the project.
# Deliberately unanchored: a workspace's storage directory can be any folder the
# user picks, so `onehand-workspace.toml` can land at any depth, not just here.
onehand.toml
onehand-workspace.toml
/ws00/

# Claude Code settings are per-machine permission allowlists, full of absolute
# home paths, which are worth nothing to anyone else.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Cargo.lock is intentionally kept (binary crate) — do NOT ignore it.

localDocs
